# Ignore auto-bootstrapped build files from common template
**/src/Makefile
**/src/linkfile
**/src/hdr.asm
**/src/data.asm
**/src/pvsneslibfont.bmp

# Ignore compiled intermediate files and assembler output
**/src/*.obj
**/src/*.asm
**/src/*.ps

# ...but Void Serpent ships its own data.asm, because it .incbin's sprite
# graphics that common/data.asm does not provide. If this were left ignored, a
# fresh clone would bootstrap the plain template and silently build a ROM with
# no sprite art at all (see CAVEATS.md section 3).
!**/void-serpent/src/data.asm

# Ignore graphics GENERATED by void-serpent/tools/gengfx.py. The art source of
# truth is the ASCII tiles inside that script; build.sh regenerates these before
# compiling, so they must never be committed (stale binaries in source control
# silently desync from the art).
**/void-serpent/src/gfx.h
**/void-serpent/src/gfx/
**/src/*.sym
**/src/*.pic
**/src/*.pal

# Ignore built ROM files (optional, but standard for build artifacts)
**/build/

# Python bytecode caches produced by the tools/ asset scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
